<title>INDIA: India's Times Bank reduces prime lending rate.</title>
<headline>India's Times Bank reduces prime lending rate.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1997-04-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>The private Times Bank said it reduced its prime lending rate to 15.5 percent per annum from 17.0 percent, a bank official said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>The new rates took effect on April 28, he said.</p>
<p>-- Bombay newsroom +91-22-265 9000</p>
</text>
